From: rive
Subject: [PATCH 0057] meet a fault wasm did not cause as the process would have

When no handler sat below wamr's, a fault outside wasm ended in abort()
inside wamr's handler. A crash reporter that only steps in once a signal
goes unhandled, such as Crashpad on macOS, then reported every crash of
the host as an abort in signal_callback. wamr now puts the default back,
even over an ignored disposition, where the fault would happen again
forever, so the process dies of the fault. On Linux a fault happens again
where it was when the handler returns, and a signal that was sent is sent
once more. macOS gives a sent signal the codes of a fault, so there every
signal is sent once more; the kernel keeps the fault the thread took, and
the crash reports it.

--- a/core/shared/platform/common/posix/posix_thread.c
+++ b/core/shared/platform/common/posix/posix_thread.c
@@ -597,6 +597,21 @@ mask_signals(int how)
 static struct sigaction prev_sig_act_SIGSEGV;
 static struct sigaction prev_sig_act_SIGBUS;
 
+/* rive patch: whether the signal happens again when the handler returns.
+   macOS gives a sent signal the codes of a fault, so there it is always
+   sent again, and the crash still records the fault the thread took. Linux
+   codes are positive only for signals the kernel raised. */
+static bool
+signal_recurs(const siginfo_t *sig_info)
+{
+#if defined(__APPLE__)
+    (void)sig_info;
+    return false;
+#else
+    return sig_info->si_code > 0;
+#endif
+}
+
 /*
  * ASAN is not designed to work with custom stack unwind or other low-level
  * things. Ignore a function that does some low-level magic. (e.g. walking
@@ -637,6 +652,8 @@ signal_callback(int sig_num, siginfo_t *sig_info, void *sig_ucontext)
     }
     /* Output signal info and then crash if signal is unhandled */
     else {
+        struct sigaction default_act;
+
         switch (sig_num) {
             case SIGSEGV:
                 os_printf("unhandled SIGSEGV, si_addr: %p\n", sig_addr);
@@ -650,7 +667,15 @@ signal_callback(int sig_num, siginfo_t *sig_info, void *sig_ucontext)
                 break;
         }
 
-        abort();
+        /* rive patch: the default ends the process at the fault, so a crash
+           reporter that waits for it to go unhandled reports it there, not
+           as an abort here. An ignored fault would happen again forever. */
+        memset(&default_act, 0, sizeof(default_act));
+        default_act.sa_handler = SIG_DFL;
+        if (sigaction(sig_num, &default_act, NULL) != 0)
+            abort();
+        if (!signal_recurs(sig_info))
+            raise(sig_num);
     }
 }
 
